@startuml
title Smart Campus Study Room Booking - Domain Class Diagram
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members

class Student {
  - studentId : String
  - name : String
}

class Room {
  - roomId : String
  - name : String
  - blocked : Boolean
  + isBlocked() : Boolean
  + block() : void
  + unblock() : void
  + isAvailable(startTime : DateTime, endTime : DateTime) : Boolean
}

class Booking {
  - bookingId : String
  - startTime : DateTime
  - endTime : DateTime
  - status : BookingStatus
  - confirmationCode : String
  - /duration : Duration
  + isActive() : Boolean
  + overlaps(startTime : DateTime, endTime : DateTime) : Boolean
  + cancel() : void
}

enum BookingStatus {
  ACTIVE
  CANCELLED
}

Student "1" -- "0..*" Booking : makes >
Room "1" -- "0..*" Booking : is reserved by >

note right of Student
  name is assumed for display only; no story
  or rule requires it (registration is out of scope).
  bookRoom() / cancelBooking() are NOT Student
  operations — BookingService runs both workflows
  (see sequence.puml). cancelBooking only succeeds
  if the booking belongs to the requesting student.
end note

note right of Room
  name is assumed for display only; no story or
  rule requires it.
  isAvailable(startTime, endTime) is the US-01 query:
  false if blocked (R3) or any ACTIVE booking overlaps
  (R2). The booking flow (sequence.puml) does NOT call
  isAvailable() directly — it needs blocked/overlap as
  separate reasons for its reply, so it uses isBlocked()
  and each booking's overlaps() individually instead.
  block() sets blocked = true only; existing ACTIVE
  bookings are not changed (declared decision).
end note

note right of Booking
  R1 (checked at creation only): startTime is after now,
  and 0 < /duration <= 2 hours.
  R2: active bookings for the same room may not overlap.
  overlaps(startTime, endTime) compares this ACTIVE
  booking against a candidate slot; a booking that ends
  exactly when another begins is NOT an overlap.
  CANCELLED bookings are excluded from the R2 check.
  US-06 (usage review) is derived from existing Booking
  data (startTime, endTime, status) filtered by period;
  it needs no class of its own.
end note
@enduml